    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented and why.\n\n## Change: `bulkSignupWarning` on owner responses\n\nWhen more than 80 owners already share a new owner's registration date, the owner's response now carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n### Files touched (5)\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `bulk_signup_warning` column with a null-safe getter (`null \u2192 false`) and a setter. No existing method changed.\n3. **`BulkSignups.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper mirroring the existing `Namesakes`/`CityCodes` idiom: `exceededDailyLimit(existing, candidate)` counts owners sharing the candidate's registration date and returns `count > 80`.\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line delegating to the helper, alongside the existing `assignCustomerCode`/`setNamesakeCount` calls. No new branch, so the method's complexity is unchanged.\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the column and the matching positional seed value (only the hsqldb schema is kept complete in this project; it's the `ddl-auto=none` test DB).\n\n### Design notes\n- MapStruct auto-maps `bulkSignupWarning` by name (like `initials`), so **no mapper change** was needed.\n- I first tried a Hibernate `@Formula` (zero controller/schema changes), but it fails under the test harness's single-transaction model: the just-created owner is returned from the persistence-context cache without a re-SELECT, so a formula (computed only on SELECT) stays null. A native query confirmed the DB logic was right, but the cached instance won. Persisting the value at creation is correct in every transaction model.\n- I verified the actual `>80` branch with a temporary test (82nd owner \u2192 `true`, 81st \u2192 `false`), then removed it.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the only edited method (`addOwner`) gained a single non-branching line, all real logic lives in a new self-contained helper with near-zero surrounding complexity, and no other function was modified.",
